WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
[Instrumental music and designed paper/interface cues; no spoken narration]
Month-end. The owner’s controls manager must reconcile scope, schedule, cost and work-package records.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Contractors expect payment. Leadership needs a clear basis for reviewing the payment applications.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
If activities appear behind schedule, why are we paying so much? Are these records describing the same work?

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
The records may each be valid. Their codes and scope boundaries can still differ.

5
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.000
WBS LINK relates each source through the Owner WBS, preserving its evidence and decision authority.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Here, a cost relationship is absent. Uncertainty stays visible. Professional decisions and whole-version approval remain separate.

7
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Confirm whether the missing governed relationship is expected or requires project-controls attention. Keep that Action linked to its original evidence.

8
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Follow the source-to-report workflow in Video 2, including professional review and separate version approval.

